## Known Gotchas

**Hash sections in the sitemap** — `src/app/sitemap.js` currently lists `/#about`, `/#services`, etc. Search engines do not index hash fragments as separate pages. The sitemap should only contain the base URL (`https://metrogaragesolutions.com`). Do not add more hash-based URLs to the sitemap.

**`nocache: true` in robots config** — set in `layout.js`. This tells Google not to store a cached copy of the page. Acceptable for a frequently updated business site but worth noting when debugging Search Console issues.

**`viewport` meta tag is manually set in `<head>`** — layout.js has `<meta name="viewport" ...>` inline. In Next.js 14+, viewport should be a separate `export const viewport` in `layout.js`. Harmless for now but should be migrated if other viewport settings are needed.

**React 19 RC** — the app uses `react@19.0.0-rc-*`. The stable React 19 APIs work the same way; just be aware if any third-party SEO library claims incompatibility.

---

## Adding New Pages

This is currently a single-page app. If route segments are added (e.g. `/services/garage-door-repair`):

1. Add a `metadata` export to the new `page.js` — don't rely solely on the root layout metadata.
2. Switch the root layout `title` to a template (see above).
3. Add the new URL to `sitemap.js` (not as a hash).
4. Add a `BreadcrumbList` schema for the new route in `StructuredData.jsx` or a local schema component.

---

## Updating FAQ Schema

The FAQ schema in `StructuredData.jsx` must match the visible FAQ content in `src/app/components/FAQ.jsx`. If FAQ questions are added or changed, update both the component text and the `faqSchema.mainEntity` array — they must stay in sync for Google's Rich Results validation.

